{"post": true, "caption": "The US 10-year Treasury yield closed near 5.3% on Oct 1, its highest level since 2002. The 30-year hit about 5.67%.\nWhen safe US bonds pay this much, money tends to flow toward the dollar.\nThat can pressure the peso and push borrowing costs higher at home.\nWatch rates before you watch price.\n\nEducation only. Not financial advice.\n\n#CandleAndCode #MarketIn20Seconds #InterestRates #Bonds #TradingEducation", "tag": "MARKET IN 20 SECONDS", "footer": "Education only. Not financial advice.", "bpm": 100, "scenes": [{"type": "hook", "dur": 2.4, "size": 120, "lines": [{"t": "US 10Y YIELD", "c": "fg"}, {"t": "5.3%", "c": "red"}, {"t": "24-YEAR HIGH", "c": "red"}]}, {"type": "text", "dur": 3.0, "lines": [{"t": "Highest since 2002.", "c": "fg"}, {"t": "It hits your wallet.", "c": "green"}], "size": 84}, {"type": "bars", "dur": 5.0, "title": "US borrowing costs", "subtitle": "Oct 1 close, highest since 2002", "rows": [{"l": "10-YEAR", "v": 5.33, "vl": "5.33%", "lc": "fg", "bc": "red"}, {"l": "30-YEAR", "v": 5.67, "vl": "5.67%", "lc": "fg", "bc": "red"}]}, {"type": "text", "dur": 3.0, "lines": [{"t": "US bonds pay more.", "c": "fg"}, {"t": "Money runs to USD.", "c": "muted"}], "size": 84}, {"type": "text", "dur": 3.2, "lines": [{"t": "That can squeeze", "c": "red"}, {"t": "the peso.", "c": "red"}, {"t": "And lift loan rates.", "c": "fg"}], "size": 84}, {"type": "text", "dur": 3.0, "lines": [{"t": "Rates move first.", "c": "fg"}, {"t": "Prices move next.", "c": "green"}], "size": 84}, {"type": "end", "dur": 2.2, "line": "Trade with a system, not a feeling."}]}